 {
  "coord": "17:19",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "hedge",
  "note": "\"might lead\" became \"would lead\".",
  "replacement": "Melians. But we know that the fortune of war is sometimes more impartial than the disproportion of numbers might lead one to suppose. To submit is to give ourselves over to despair, while action still preserves for us a hope that we may stand erect."
 },
 {
  "coord": "17:20",
  "verdict": "PASS",
  "note": "Faithful."
 },
 {
  "coord": "17:21",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "hedge",
  "note": "\"may grant\" became the stronger \"will grant\".",
  "replacement": "Melians. You may be sure that we are as well aware as you how hard it is to contend against your power and fortune, unless the terms are equal. But we trust that the gods may grant us fortune as good as yours, because we are just men fighting against unjust. And we trust that what we lack in power will be made up by the alliance of the Lacedaemonians, who are bound, if only for very shame, to come to the aid of their kindred. So our confidence, after all, is not so utterly irrational."
 },
